# PCI deployment integration

Deployment content of FACIS FAP Principal Credential Issuance (PCI) release
`{{VERSION}}`, generated from source commit
[`{{COMMIT}}`]({{SOURCE}}/tree/{{COMMIT}}) of the
[PCI repository]({{SOURCE}}) by `tools/export-deployment-package.mjs`.
Application source, application tests, release records, specification documents
and the application CI remain in the PCI repository. Do not edit the files of this
directory by hand: change them in the PCI repository and export the package again;
[SOURCE.json](SOURCE.json) records the hash every file had in the source and the
adaptations made by the export.

## Contents

- Helm charts: `deployment/helm/fap-pci` (PCI prerequisite objects generated by
  ground-zero), `deployment/helm/participant` (participant data service),
  `deployment/helm/observability` (private telemetry).
- Ground-zero setup (`dist/ground-zero.sh`), flow and UI artifacts (`dist/`),
  the flow/UI installer and ownership-aware uninstall (`automation/stage1/`),
  lifecycle automation (`scripts/lifecycle.py`, `automation/`).
- Identity, participant and transport helpers (`scripts/`), the all-hop TLS
  profile (`deployment/prerequisites/`), the ArgoCD example
  (`deployment/argocd/`).
- The images of this release, pinned by digest: [deployment/images.json](deployment/images.json).
- Operator documentation under `docs/`: [deployment](docs/operations/deployment.md),
  [backup and rollback](docs/operations/backup-rollback.md),
  [troubleshooting and FAQ](docs/operations/troubleshooting.md),
  [runbook](docs/operations/runbook.md).

## Verify

```bash
cd PCI
sha256sum --strict -c deployment-sha256.txt
```

## Deploy

Follow this repository's `basic-cluster-init.sh` and `ocm-wstack-init.sh` sequence for
the shared stack, then the [PCI deployment guide](docs/operations/deployment.md): G0
prepares the PCI ORCE deployment, configuration, database and Gateway routes; the ORCE
container then runs the application image of `deployment/images.json` by digest, or
the flows and UI of `dist/` are installed with `automation/stage1/install.sh`. Take the
backup of [backup and rollback](docs/operations/backup-rollback.md) before an upgrade.
Record every deployment with `scripts/record-deployment.py`.

Required operator tools: Bash, Python 3, Node.js 20+, kubectl, Helm 3.17+, jq, curl,
OpenSSL, tar, base64 and sha256sum; PyYAML 6.0.2 for the optional mesh inventory.
Keep completed private inputs (kubeconfig, certificates, lifecycle configuration)
outside Git.

## Change process

This directory changes only through a pull request that carries a new export, reviewed
under the rules of this repository and merged by its maintainers. The pull request
names the PCI release, its tag and commit, and the PCI pull requests it carries.
